00:25:02,860 --> 00:25:12,860
You should probably be looking at
increasing the amount of positions in your
portfolio by double, so by 100%.

158
00:25:12,860 --> 00:25:19,860
And then take the portfolio based
approach, put cash to work in a well
diversified long short portfolio.

159
00:25:19,860 --> 00:25:29,860
So again, there's no hard and fast rules
telling you exactly what you can and can't
do when the VIX goes up or down
aggressively.

160
00:25:29,860 --> 00:25:32,860
Everyone's risk tolerance is different.

161
00:25:32,860 --> 00:25:34,860
Everyone's strategies are different.

162
00:25:34,860 --> 00:25:38,860
And everyone's portfolio looks different
and is made up differently.

163
00:25:38,860 --> 00:25:48,860
So when the VIX does rally aggressively,
you've got to interpret what's happening
in the world at the time and why it's
going up so fast.

164
00:25:48,860 --> 00:26:01,860
And then if you don't like the volatility
risk, then just reduce your portfolio,
reduce your exposure because you need to
understand again that as the VIX is going
up, the world's portfolio risk is going up
and so is yours.

165
00:26:01,860 --> 00:26:07,860
And it's going up and there's nothing you
can do about it unless you actually go and
reduce your exposure.

166
00:26:08,860 --> 00:26:16,860
And then when the opposite occurs, so when
the VIX is falling aggressively, you've
got to interpret what's happening and why
it's falling so fast.

167
00:26:17,860 --> 00:26:24,860
It'll be falling fast because something
will have occurred that takes away the
risk in the market.

168
00:26:24,860 --> 00:26:37,860
And you're going to be told by when you're
