and political only.

331
00:47:17,860 --> 00:47:29,860
So when you trade a specific currency,
it's because a macroeconomic condition has
occurred which affects that specific
country.

332
00:47:29,860 --> 00:47:49,860
In commodities, it's broadly macro, but if
you get micro news flow that specifically
affects that particular commodity where it
affects the supply chain, you're going to
have opportunities to day trade it.

333
00:47:49,860 --> 00:48:02,860
And examples of this would be, for
example, the Energy Information
Administration in the US when they release
the inventories data for oil on a
Wednesday.

334
00:48:02,860 --> 00:48:08,860
And you get big moves versus expectations
in inventory builds.

335
00:48:08,860 --> 00:48:15,860
And that is basically affecting the supply
chain, but not necessarily at a macro
level.

336
00:48:15,860 --> 00:48:19,860
There's been interference in the market.

337
00:48:19,860 --> 00:48:20,860
That's unexpected.

338
00:48:20,860 --> 00:48:24,860
And you can day trade oil on the back of
those situations.

339
00:48:24,860 --> 00:48:30,860
Other good examples of this would be, for
example, in the food commodity space.

340
00:48:30,860 --> 00:48:43,860
So in the grains like corn, wheat, in
pulses like soybean, in livestock like
cattle and hogs.

341
00:48:43,860 --> 00:48:58,860
If you get microeconomic factors affecting
the supply chain in those commodities, you
can make good money day trading.

342
00:48:58,860 --> 00:49:00,860
You'll see a lot of volatility around.

343
00:49:00,860 --> 00:49:18,860
So, you know, good examples of this were
in 2012 in the food commodities, where
there was a heat wave in the United
States, and we had some of the lowest
corn, wheat and soybean crops for a
generation.

344
00:49:18,860 --> 00:49:22,860
And the weather really affected the supply
chain.

345
00:49:22,860 --> 00:49:36,860
And a lot of people made really good money
jumping into corn very quickly and day
trading it from the long side, and wheat
and in soybean as well.

346
00:49:36,860 --> 00:49:50,860
And, in fact, if you'd have just run those
positions over the summer, you'd have made
a lot of money in those three instruments,
in those three commodities, because the
trend actually continued for a good few
months.

347
00:49:50,860 --> 00:50:03,860
In bonds and rates, we've only got
macroeconomic and political news that
really affects the bond market and rates
in a particular geographical region or
country.

348
00:50:03,860 --> 00:50:12,860
Micro factors really affect stocks the
most, where you've got situations that
affect particular supply chains.

349
00:50:12,860 --> 00:50:26,860
So a good example of where the VIX went up
significantly and at the same time you had
micro factors affecting the value chain in
a particular industry.

350
00:50:26,860 --> 00:50:33,860
And unique news that was affecting that
industry and stocks within the industry.

351
00:50:33,860 --> 00:50:41,860
A very good example of that was the
earthquake in Japan in 2011.

352
00:50:41,860 --> 00:50:52,860
Because with the earthquake in the
northeast of Japan, what you got was the
tech supply chain effectively being wiped
out in Japan.

353
00:50:52,860 --> 00:50:58,860
And technology companies had to move all
of their supply chain to Thailand.

354
00:50:58,860 --> 00:51:01,860
A lot of companies had to do that.

355
00:51:01,860 --> 00:51:05,860
And then you also had the Thai floods
later in the year.

356
00:51:05,860 --> 00:51:13,860
So there were some big day trading
opportunities or short term opportunities
in the US tech sector and the tech sector
as a whole globally.

357
00:51:13,860 --> 00:51:20,860
So if you get all of those three things
lined up, that's where the big
opportunities occur in short term trading.

358
00:51:20,860 --> 00:51:23,860
And that was a really good example of
that.

359
00:51:23,860 --> 00:51:25,860
And usually you get these opportunities at
least once a year.

360
00:51:25,860 --> 00:51:27,860
So you've got to keep an eye out for them.

361
00:51:27,860 --> 00:51:34,860
Now what about connecting the dots and how
we hunt for volatility?

362
00:51:34,860 --> 00:51:43,860
Well, when we get to asset specific news
flow, there's really five areas that we
need to consider.

363
00:51:43,860 --> 00:51:46,860
We need to consider the results of
companies.

364
00:51:46,860 --> 00:51:50,860
So earnings announcements and profit
warnings.

365
00:51:50,860 --> 00:52:04,860
So when companies materially miss their
expected earnings numbers by the market or
they meet them and they warn on future
earnings.

366
00:52:04,860 --> 00:52:08,860
So the market now has to downgrade their
expectations.

367
00:52:08,860 --> 00:52:09,860
Bid rumors.

368
00:52:09,860 --> 00:52:15,860
So where there's rumors around that a
company is going to be bought by another
company.

369
00:52:15,860 --> 00:52:22,860
Unique events that no one could foresee
like a CEO dying in a car crash.

370
00:52:22,860 --> 00:52:24,860
No one can ever see that coming.

371
00:52:24,860 --> 00:52:25,860
And sentiment.

372
00:52:25,860 --> 00:52:27,860
So big shifts in sentiment.

373
00:52:27,860 --> 00:52:40,860
And big shifts in sentiment we mean by the
market now views an asset totally
differently because some unexpected news
has occurred.

374
00:52:40,860 --> 00:52:45,860
Knowing your asset.

375
00:52:45,860 --> 00:52:50,860
So this is pretty important stuff.

376
00:52:50,860 --> 00:52:52,860
We're going to use some examples here.

377
00:52:52,860 --> 00:52:57,860
We're going to use some examples from the
United Kingdom.

378
00:52:57,860 --> 00:53:03,860
And we're going to go through a variance
of ATR.

379
00:53:03,860 --> 00:53:05,860
So a variance of average true range.

380
00:53:05,860 --> 00:53:14,860
So this is what you should really do to
understand if you're about to day trade
something.

381
00:53:14,860 --> 00:53:22,860
If you're about to go into the market and
take a position on a day trade or a short
term trade.

382
00:53:22,860 --> 00:53:29,860
This is the exercise that you should
really be doing once you've decided, OK,
I'm going to day trade this asset now.

383
00:53:29,860 --> 00:53:32,860
And a lot of people go in unprepared.

384
00:53:32,860 --> 00:53:38,860
So I would say the first thing that you've
