398
00:54:47,860 --> 00:54:50,860
And the average open to low move.

399
00:54:52,860 --> 00:54:59,860
And then we're looking at the average
daily move close to close on a one day
basis over this period.

400
00:54:59,860 --> 00:55:07,860
And you should work this stuff out just so
you can, one, manage your expectations,
but also set stop losses and targets
correctly.

401
00:55:07,860 --> 00:55:14,860
So first thing we're going to look at is
the Barclays volatility open to high.

402
00:55:14,860 --> 00:55:16,860
So this is a variance of the ATR.

403
00:55:16,860 --> 00:55:19,860
So we're only looking at the upside here.

404
00:55:19,860 --> 00:55:22,860
And here we're looking at the downside.

405
00:55:22,860 --> 00:55:32,860
So where the stock opens relative to where
its trading high is on a day going back
over a year.

406
00:55:32,860 --> 00:55:49,860
And you can see very, very rarely does
Barclays have a day where it goes over
from open to trading high over 10p or 10p
in the UK.

407
00:55:51,860 --> 00:56:02,860
And if you're going into the market in the
morning and you see materially positive
news and you think it's going to be a
really significant opportunity for day
trading.

408
00:56:02,860 --> 00:56:20,860
Well, your opportunity to actually buy
Barclays from where it opens, you need to
be clearly buying the stock from where it
opens within at least 4p from where it
opens.

409
00:56:21,860 --> 00:56:32,860
And have a stop loss and a realistic
target because very rarely does this stock
actually go up above a 10p difference from
the price that it opens.

410
00:56:32,860 --> 00:56:35,860
So manage your expectations, firstly.

411
00:56:35,860 --> 00:56:39,860
Secondly, set stop losses and targets
accordingly.

412
00:56:39,860 --> 00:56:45,860
And we can see here the average open to
